**Given:**

The speed from A to B = 200 kmph

The speed from B to A = 300 kmph

**Concept:**

Average speed={Total distanceover Total time}

**Formula used:**

Speed ={Distance over Time}

**Calculation:**

Let the average speed of both side of the travel be X and distance be D

The time taken by man from A to B = {Dover200}

The time taken by man from B to A = {Dover300}

The total time taken by man = {Dover200}+{Dover300}={3D+2Dover600} = {5Dover600} = {Dover120}

The average speed of the man = {2Dover{Dover120}}= {120×2}= 240 kmph

**∴ The required result will be 240 kmph.**
